    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Subject: Request for Parental Priority in Comprehensive Sexuality Education\n\nDear School Board Members,\n\nI am writing as a concerned parent to express my strong disagreement with the current push for a one-size-fits-all comprehensive sexuality education curriculum. While I support open dialogue and age-appropriate information, I firmly believe that the final decision regarding the depth and specific details of sensitive topics lies exclusively with parents, not the school district.\n\nIt is a fundamental right for families to guide their children through matters of health and relationships in ways that align with their values and upbringing. Allowing a single mandate to dictate these critical family lessons ignores the diverse moral and religious backgrounds of our community and oversteps the proper boundary between public education and private family influence. We urge the board to either significantly delay implementation until we can collaborate on a less intrusive approach or immediately revert to a model that prioritizes individual parental authority over any district-wide curriculum.\n\nSincerely,\n\n[Your Name]\n[Your Address/Contact Information]\n[Optional: Parent of specific child, optional but firm]",
      "source": "target",
